# Everyday Cool Arcade — game manifest
# One line per game, pipe-separated:
#   slug | collection project folder | game file | lesson file (or -) | extra files (comma-separated, or -) | display title
# Paths are relative to the collection's projects/ directory and the
# game's own project folder. The game file and its lesson are copied as
# siblings into dist/games/<slug>/ so the relative links between them
# (including the in-game lesson pop-ups) work unchanged. Extra files are
# support files a game page needs (Stack-a-Bot lives inside the Games
# Room page and brings its scripts and styles along). The display title
# is the game's name as players see it; tools/sync-dist.sh reads it to
# generate the Game Documents page (dist/documents.html), so a game
# added here brings its document link with it.
siege-demolition|everyday-physics|siege-demolition.html|siege-demolition-lesson.html|-|Siege Slingshot Demolition
